@<Language@/C@/Module@/Interface@/wrap with included flag@=
@<Tool@/Text Processing@/basic python settings@>


class ModuleMeta(pydantic.BaseModel):
    model_config = pydantic.ConfigDict(extra='allow')
    name: str
    included_flag_format: str


meta = configuration(ModuleMeta, r'''
@<..@/Meta@/module meta information@>
''')
flag = meta.included_flag_format % meta.name.upper()
sys.stdout.write(f'#ifndef {flag}\n#define {flag}\n')
sys.stdout.write(sys.stdin.read())
sys.stdout.write('#endif\n')
@
The module meta information is a Jsonnet object.
The module properties are the fields of a second object, which override these defaults;
Jsonnet rejects a field given twice in the module properties.
@<Language@/C@/Module@/Meta@/module meta information@=
{
    name: 'default',
    included_flag_format: '_MODULE_%s',
} + {
    @<..@/module properties@>
}
