print(usage.replace('\\', r'\\').replace('"', r'\"').replace('\n', r'\n'), end='')
@|Tool@/evaluate@
Light reflects the author's preferences and customs,
which includes how to format code,
how to manage memory, how to handle exception, etc.
It also supports some common data structures.

- `light.h`: the generated header;
- `light.c`: the generated implementation;
- `light options`: compile-time options;
- `light@@:executable@@:C Structure@@/module`: an executable using the framework;
- `light-single@@:executable@@:C Structure@@/module`: a single-file executable using the framework.

