The import path of a package is the module path joined with its directory.
Reference it with the package label, inside quotes in import paths.
A command needs no directory here, because no package imports a command.
@<Language@/Go@/Module@/import path@=
@<Tool@/Text Processing@/basic python settings@>
directory = r'''
@<.@/package directory@>
'''.strip(' \t\n\r\f\v')
if (re.search(r'^/|/$|//|\s', directory)
        or any(part in ('.', '..') for part in directory.split('/'))):
    fail(f"package directory '{directory}' is not valid")
module = '@<.@/Meta@/module path@>'
print(f'{module}/{directory}' if directory else module, end='')
