The package directory is the path of a package below the module root, without a leading slash.
A package sets it under the package label.
The package at the module root keeps the empty directory.
@<Language@/Go@/Module@/package directory@=@
A requirement is one line of the require block: a module path and a version.
No require block is emitted when the list is empty or contains only whitespace.
Only blank lines are removed before the first requirement,
so every requirement keeps its indentation.
A project with requirements also declares go.sum in the file set go module,
because the checks never rewrite go.mod or go.sum.
@<Language@/Go@/Module@/go.mod@=
@<Tool@/Text Processing@/basic python settings@>
@<.@/Meta@/project meta model@>


meta = configuration(ProjectMeta, r'''
@<.@/Meta@/project meta information@>
''')
requirements = re.sub(r'\A\s*\n', '', r'''
@<.@/requirements@>
''').rstrip(' \t\n\r\f\v')
print(f'module {meta.module}\n\ngo {meta.go}')
if requirements:
    print(f'\nrequire (\n{requirements}\n)')
@|Tool@/evaluate@
@<Language@/Go@/Module@/Meta@/module path@=
